    }
}
```
Reason:
The `term_mode_init()` function call was placed after the check for the `DTE_FORCE_TERMINFO` environment variable, which means that if this variable is set, the terminal mode may not be initialized before other terminal initialization logic is executed. This can lead to failures when trying to get terminal attributes, as the terminal mode would not be set up properly.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!term_mode_init()) {
    term_init_fail("tcgetattr: %s", strerror(errno));
}
```
Reason:
By moving the `term_mode_init()` function call to occur before the check for `DTE_FORCE_TERMINFO`, the terminal mode is initialized correctly before any other terminal initialization logic is executed. This ensures that the terminal attributes can be retrieved successfully, preventing the failures that were occurring previously.

